On Mon, 05 Mar 2007 04:59:43 +0100, <masquerade808@gmail.com> wrote:

> I played NetHack for a long time before stumbling upon SLASH'EM, and
> although I do enjoy it, I find that a few things in the game are
> rather mechanically quirky. For instance, the Doppleganger class seems
> terribly random, the Necromancer is absurdly weak until an extremely
> high level, and even though favorite classes recieved nice little
> additions in the form of techniques (even though I miss the Rogue's
> daggers), one thing has bothered me to no end.
>
> Vampires in SLASH'EM seem extremely weak. Their special abilities can
> be handy, but this is ruined by the fact that vampires tend to die of
> starvation on Dlvl 3. Can anyone give advice on how to play SLASH'EM
> Vampires?

Fighters Vampire might be better since spellcasting cause hunger and  
killing with spells prevent bitting. I've managed a barbarian Vampire  
quite far away.
An early medecine bag is great because you can then self level-drain (less  
dangerous monsters) and get food... If you also find a coaligned altar,  
bingo !
#pray for food, as said.
Don't waste time in shops (especially in the mall) until you get ring of  
SD or similar stuff... Of course the ring might be in the shop but, well,  
just go for the rings in shops and when you can identify them.
Using your pet to rob a shop is far too slow for a Vampire until he has an  
easy way of feeding.
The chaotic quest might provide lots of food carried by all these  
vampires... But of course there is the problem of Vecna (potion of  
paralysis, boulder fort and +7 silver bullets, ...)

Level drain resistance is great (wands of draining !) and intrinsic flying  
very useful by the end (create pools is a real pain).

